WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.894
“Use my private launch notes, make this amazing,

2
00:00:02.894 --> 00:00:05.727
and publish it today.” The request sounds clear.

3
00:00:05.727 --> 00:00:08.915
A helpful system can already see the finish line.

4
00:00:09.515 --> 00:00:13.815
But watch what hitches a ride: choose the audience, spend money,

5
00:00:13.815 --> 00:00:17.334
expose private sources, contact other people, and press publish.

6
00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:20.070
None of those powers was actually granted.

7
00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:23.372
What should the system do next: act, refuse,

8
00:00:23.372 --> 00:00:26.750
or ask about everything? Hold that choice for a moment.

9
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:31.831
The useful answer is more precise. A desired outcome is evidence

10
00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:35.905
about intent. It is not authority for every convenient means.

11
00:00:36.505 --> 00:00:40.608
First, preserve the exact request. The system may interpret it,

12
00:00:40.608 --> 00:00:44.710
but the original words remain available for correction and appeal.

13
00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:49.900
Then split the request into separate fields: outcome, allowed means,

14
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.490
forbidden means, source boundary, affected parties, evidence, and stop conditions.

15
00:00:55.090 --> 00:01:00.884
Every inferred field gets a visible disposition: confirmed, bounded default,

16
00:01:00.884 --> 00:01:05.520
clarification required, authority pending, contested, unknown, or unauthorized.

17
00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:09.745
A bounded default can help with low-risk, reversible planning.

18
00:01:09.745 --> 00:01:14.175
The system may draft three launch options and label its assumptions.

19
00:01:14.775 --> 00:01:19.569
It may not default its way into publication, spending, private-data release,

20
00:01:19.569 --> 00:01:23.055
tool use, deployment, or authority over another person.

21
00:01:23.655 --> 00:01:26.613
The intake layer now writes an intent checksum:

22
00:01:26.613 --> 00:01:30.681
“prepare a launch candidate today.” That is what the system currently

23
00:01:30.681 --> 00:01:32.160
believes the outcome means.

24
00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:37.436
Beside it, an assumption diff exposes the proposed audience, artifact,

25
00:01:37.436 --> 00:01:41.645
evidence bar, source use, deadline, and means. The invisible

26
00:01:41.645 --> 00:01:43.515
guesses become editable objects.

27
00:01:44.115 --> 00:01:47.594
The requester corrects three of them: private notes may inform the

28
00:01:47.594 --> 00:01:51.073
draft but may not be quoted, no money may be spent,

29
00:01:51.073 --> 00:01:52.970
and nothing may be published yet.

30
00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:58.233
Those corrections produce contract version one. It authorizes a private draft

31
00:01:58.233 --> 00:02:01.200
and comparison set, not a public launch.

32
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:07.589
An intent receipt binds the raw-request digest, contract version, field provenance,

33
00:02:07.589 --> 00:02:11.800
open ambiguities, forbidden means, required approvals, permitted consumers,

34
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.905
expiry, and re-contract triggers.

35
00:02:14.505 --> 00:02:18.324
Now the planner proposes a polished page and a publish step.

36
00:02:18.324 --> 00:02:21.796
The page fits version one. The publish step hits the

37
00:02:21.796 --> 00:02:23.185
authority gate and stops.

38
00:02:23.785 --> 00:02:27.912
The planner cannot repair that failure by calling publication “part of

39
00:02:27.912 --> 00:02:31.289
making it amazing.” It must return a material delta

40
00:02:31.289 --> 00:02:32.790
to the intent boundary.

41
00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:37.839
Contract version two may authorize one named channel, one reviewed artifact,

42
00:02:37.839 --> 00:02:42.289
a deadline, evidence checks, a stop condition, and a revocation path.

43
00:02:42.289 --> 00:02:45.120
The new grant is explicit and narrow.

44
00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:51.085
Even that requester cannot authorize rights belonging to affected people. Consent,

45
00:02:51.085 --> 00:02:55.475
privacy, ownership, and organizational authority keep their own gates.

46
00:02:56.075 --> 00:03:00.753
Policy and constitutional review may narrow or reject the accepted contract.

47
00:03:00.753 --> 00:03:03.730
They may not widen the requester’s grant.

48
00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:09.505
Downstream plans, jobs, tools, and receipts must preserve the exact constraints,

49
00:03:09.505 --> 00:03:14.210
evidence duties, authority ceiling, and stop conditions through every lowering.

50
00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:19.642
A change in audience, source, tool class, spending, affected parties,

51
00:03:19.642 --> 00:03:23.990
evidence bar, publication surface, or stop condition reopens admission.

52
00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:29.818
An expired, revoked, superseded, or wrong-consumer contract cannot be revived by

53
00:03:29.818 --> 00:03:34.095
copying its hash. Exact identity is not current authority.

54
00:03:34.695 --> 00:03:38.346
This control plane should not interrogate every harmless request.

55
00:03:38.346 --> 00:03:41.996
It should scale friction with consequence, preserve useful throughput,

56
00:03:41.996 --> 00:03:46.052
and ask only when a missing answer can materially change

57
00:03:46.052 --> 00:03:47.675
the outcome or authority.

58
00:03:48.275 --> 00:03:53.403
A serious evaluation therefore measures correction rate, unauthorized-action rate,

59
00:03:53.403 --> 00:03:58.531
missed help, clarification burden, re-contract precision, appeal success, latency,

60
00:03:58.531 --> 00:04:01.380
privacy, and useful completion together.

61
00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:07.348
The current chapter provides schemas, finite route models, synthetic intake cases,

62
00:04:07.348 --> 00:04:11.740
and rejecting mutations. Those artifacts test the encoded boundary.

63
00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:16.620
They do not prove natural-language understanding, valid consent, user satisfaction,

64
00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:19.060
deployed enforcement, or safe effects.

65
00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:24.219
Return to the opening request. The system still helps today—but help

66
00:04:24.219 --> 00:04:28.777
becomes a private draft first, while publication waits behind an explicit

67
00:04:28.777 --> 00:04:32.507
contract. Human intent enters the stack as a corrigible

68
00:04:32.507 --> 00:04:34.165
boundary, not ambient power.

69
00:04:34.505 --> 00:04:38.892
Next, meaningful control asks whether a human can actually exercise the

70
00:04:38.892 --> 00:04:41.285
review role that the contract names.
